# Agda scratch probes.  Agents testing whether something reduces on the nose
# write throwaway modules; two of these (`ZZTestSolver.agda`, `Probe1.agda`)
# were swept into commits by `git add -A` and had to be removed again.  A
# probe is a question, not a result: name it `Probe*.agda` or `Scratch*.agda`
# and it stays out of the tree.  Anything worth keeping goes in
# `NaturalMachine/` under a name that carries its category.
formal/cubical/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Tmp*.agda
formal/cubical/Scratch*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Probe*.agda
formal/cubical/**/Scratch*.agda
runtime/LIVING_RUN.log
runtime/LIVING_STATE.json
vigil-state.json
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/real_workload
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/decic_extend
zzz/natural_machine_cpu_loop_rust/root_singular_series
formal/cubical/Candidate_*.agda

# interactive/library.terms WAS tracked, on the reasoning kept below, and is
# ignored again as of 2026-08-25.  The reasoning was sound and its premise is
# gone: it named MathMachine as the reader that loads this file at startup, and
# MathMachine.hs no longer exists in this repository.  The current machine
# (Main -> Server -> ProofGate/DefectRecord) reads no repository data file at
# all except the defect log named by $DOSA_LEKHA; every other name below
# appears in the Haskell only inside comments.  Verified 2026-08-25 by
# grepping every readFile/openFile/withFile/hGetContents in interactive/*.hs.
# Nothing can compound across a clone that does not carry the file -- and
# nothing reads it, so nothing compounds either way.  The superseded note,
# kept because it records why it was tracked for eight days:
#
#   > It is the machine's MEMORY, the file MathMachine reads at startup to
#   > re-admit what earlier runs proved.  Ignored, it never left the container
#   > that wrote it, so every fresh checkout started the machine from
#   > mRules = [] and re-derived the same theorems forever.  Tracked as of
#   > 2026-08-17.

# Machine build artifacts (reproducible; never source of truth)
interactive/*.hi
interactive/*.o
interactive/arithvocab
interactive/bench-head-depth
interactive/cyclotomic-vocab
interactive/parallel-gate
interactive/library.certs
interactive/self_architecture.tsv
interactive/nested-agda/

# Certificate gate cache: re-derivable, and every entry stores the exact
# module source it certified, so it is a rebuildable artifact not a record.
interactive/.certcache/
formal/cubical/.claude/
interactive/replay.traces.live

# The sabhā: the compiled process and its transcript.  The binary is
# rebuildable from interactive/check-sabha.sh; the transcript is a session
# record, kept locally and never rewritten in place (append-only), and it
# is the corpus this wire exists to produce.
interactive/sabha
interactive/sabha.jsonl

# The interface the other carrier is handed: the compiled binary, rebuildable
# from interactive/check-karana.sh.  Its outputs (the tool schema, the training
# records) are regenerated from the running dispatch table and a transcript,
# so neither is committed either -- a committed copy would be the second copy
# that drifts, which is the thing this lane exists to remove.
interactive/karana
interactive/abhyasa.jsonl
**/.certcache/

# compiled binaries — build output, rebuilt in place by interactive/check-*.sh; never track
interactive/math-machine
interactive/repairfixpoint
interactive/question-machine

# Markdown is banned in this repository (owner, 2026-08-24).  The hook
# .claude/hooks/no-markdown.sh refuses the write; this is the second layer,
# for whatever the hook fails open on -- it fails open by design, because a
# guard that blocks what it cannot parse is an outage wearing enforcement's
# name.  3630 .md files were removed in the same change; they are in the
# history and `git show` returns every one.
#
# A .md file asserts.  A checked term is the object, and it is still there
# tomorrow.  Put it in Agda (formal/cubical/, fibre/src/) or Lean
# (formal/lean/); if it is a header or a struck claim, it belongs in the
# module it is about.
#
# The exceptions are not prose.  They are files the HARNESS LOADS as
# configuration -- deleting them removes a mechanism, not an assertion.
*.md
*.markdown
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md
!.claude/skills/**/*.md

# cabal's build tree, created in the repo root by
# scripts/Dhruva_TheDeclaredPinIsBuiltFromNothingOrTheRunSaysWhichItGot.sh
# when it builds the pinned Agda 2.8.0.  A build artifact, never a claim.
dist-newstyle/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PURIFICATION, 2026-08-25, owner: "gitignore build artifacts logs etc."
#
# Everything above this line was written one path at a time, by whoever
# happened to compile something new, which is why it lists four binaries
# by name and misses the fifth.  These are the general rules.  A build
# artifact is reproducible from a command in the tree; a log and a
# transcript are records of ONE CONTAINER and do not survive the clone
# they were written in.  Neither is a claim, and neither is source.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# compiled output, any lane, any depth
*.hi
*.o
*.agdai
*.dyn_hi
*.dyn_o
*.so
*.a

# logs and per-run transcripts
*.log
*.jsonl

# the archive is history, not working state: nothing here is built,
# checked, imported or run.  It is kept so `git log` and `git show`
# still answer, and so a claim can be traced to the script it came from.
zzz/**/*.pyc

# interactive/yantra-session.lekha — the per-run session defect log.
# run-yantra.sh does `rm -f "$LEKHA"` on EVERY invocation, by design: its
# own header says the chain must start at genesis so that `dosa.pramanya`
# verifies THIS run and not a history it did not produce.  So a committed
# copy is, by construction, always some other container's run — and a
# `--wire` session deletes it and writes nothing, which is how it showed
# up as a staged deletion.
interactive/yantra-session.lekha

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE LANE-ERA DATA FILES.  Untracked 2026-08-25, kept on disk.
#
# These are session state from the period when several lanes ran against one
# working tree: a shared defect log, a standpoint store, engine memory,
# replay traces, scratch notes.  They are records of runs, not sources.  None
# of them is read by the machine that exists now -- see the note above on
# library.terms for the check that establishes it -- and none is an input to
# `sh check`, which typechecks only formal/, fibre/ and the Lean root closure.
#
# interactive/dosa.lekha is the largest of them: 41 append-only records
# written 2026-08-20..23 by twelve different lane authors, hash-chained, each
# naming what a collapse at that site would have destroyed.  It was tracked
# because several lanes appended to it concurrently and the chain had to
# survive a clone.  There are no longer several lanes.  run-yantra.sh points
# $DOSA_LEKHA at the per-run session log above and never reads this file, so
# untracking it does not change what the machine does; it stops a 181 KB
# multi-agent transcript from being part of what the repository presents.
#
# SIX OF THESE MOVED OUT INSTEAD, on 2026-08-25, and are TRACKED at
# zzz/machine-runs/: library.terms, sanghatta-report-2026-08-23.txt,
# replay.traces, thoughts.bhavana.math, thoughts.math, mula.pramana.  They
# are cited by checked Agda modules whose CONTENT came out of a run that
# wrote them -- SeamClosed's `addZero` is transcribed verbatim from
# replay.traces record 1 -- so they are provenance, not session state, and a
# citation to a file no clone carries is not a citation.  See
# zzz/machine-runs/INDEX.  interactive/thoughts.*.math below still
# catches thoughts.pair.math and the two thoughts.upamana.* files, which no
# module cites.
#
# Kept on disk rather than deleted: `git log` still answers for all of them,
# and interactive/scripts that predate this still find them in a working
# container.  A fresh clone will not have them -- scripts/check-dosa-lekha.sh
# and the other lane runners are the ones that will notice.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
interactive/dosa.lekha
interactive/naya.kosha
interactive/library.gen1.txt
interactive/library.snapshot.txt
interactive/machine.log.gen1
interactive/nadi-saksin
interactive/repairfixpoint.cert.txt
interactive/knobs.conf
interactive/svayam-avatarana
interactive/pratikara.STRUCK
interactive/pratikara.STRUCK.*
interactive/thoughts.*.math
